  "core": "Flourishing grows what is already working well — tending, harvesting, reinvesting the yield. In Nurturing, it operates on the ground itself: soil becomes richer, seeds find better purchase, the whole system deepens. Overdone, the tending becomes endless: every harvest triggers replanting, every growth demands more growth, and the ground is never allowed to rest. The abundance exhausts what feeds it.",
  "sheetLine": "The harvest demands another planting; the soil gets no season to lie fallow."
